 "cma_new_s3": "7577",
 "hab_text": "Without DPF, PSO was worse by 5.4% for $n=10$ and 16.6% for $n=20$; with a greedy slot-by-slot choice among the same candidates instead of the dynamic program, DPF-PSO was worse by 1.6% and 3.8%, so the optimality of the recombination matters; without global fusion, it was worse by 1.8% and 8.4%; and fusion without PSO moves (DPF-only, which spends the budget on repeated fusions) was worse by 1.9% and 1.0%.",
 "swarm_gain": "The PSO moves thus add a small but significant gain to the dynamic program.",
 "disc_swarm": "The swarm adds a small but significant gain",
 "hab_zh": "PSO（n = 10：Δ̃ = +5.4%，DPF-PSO 显著更好；n = 20：Δ̃ = +16.6%，DPF-PSO 显著更好）；greedy instead of DP（n = 10：Δ̃ = +1.6%，DPF-PSO 显著更好；n = 20：Δ̃ = +3.8%，DPF-PSO 显著更好）；w/o global fusion（n = 10：Δ̃ = +1.8%，DPF-PSO 显著更好；n = 20：Δ̃ = +8.4%，DPF-PSO 显著更好）；fusion only (no PSO moves)（n = 10：Δ̃ = +1.9%，DPF-PSO 显著更好；n = 20：Δ̃ = +1.0%，DPF-PSO 显著更好）",
 "heq_text": "it was significantly better than DE for both $n$ (Δ̃ = +2.1% and +9.5%), significantly better than IDP for $n=10$ but not significantly different from it for $n=20$ (Δ̃ = +0.6% and −0.2%), and not significantly different from SPSO for either $n$ (Δ̃ = +0.1% and +4.4%).",
 "heq_zh": "SPSO（n = 10：Δ̃ = +0.1%，无显著差异；n = 20：Δ̃ = +4.4%，无显著差异）；DE（n = 10：Δ̃ = +2.1%，DPF-PSO 显著更好；n = 20：Δ̃ = +9.5%，DPF-PSO 显著更好）；IDP（n = 10：Δ̃ = +0.6%，DPF-PSO 显著更好；n = 20：Δ̃ = −0.2%，无显著差异）",
 "heq_scope": "; at equal CPU time, it was not significantly better than SPSO (either $n$) and IDP ($n=20$) on the held-out scenarios",
 "heq_weak_zh": "等 CPU 时间下，DPF-PSO 在留出场景上与 SPSO（n = 10、20）、IDP（n = 20） 无显著差异",
 "band_text": "To test this post hoc explanation, we repeated the held-out runs of SPSO, DE, IDP, DPF-PSO, tuned SPSO and tuned DPF-PSO with the band enforced exactly along every segment: a segment closer than 100 m to the ground or more than 200 m above it is penalized like a clearance violation, and its maximum height is computed with the exact clearance method on the mirrored terrain $-Z$ (supplement S4). Tuned SPSO then lost its advantage: tuned DPF-PSO was significantly better for both $n$ (Δ̃ = +2.8% and +4.6%; Table III). With default configurations, DPF-PSO was significantly better than SPSO for both $n$ (Δ̃ = +6.0% and +8.2%), significantly better than IDP for $n=10$ but not significantly different from it for $n=20$ (Δ̃ = +0.5% and −0.2%), and not significantly different from DE for $n=10$ but significantly better than it for $n=20$ (Δ̃ = −0.3% and +6.9%). All runs ended with a feasible path except 1 of the 400 runs of DE for $n=20$.",
 "abs_spso": "Tuned spherical-vector PSO was better for 10 waypoints because it can merge waypoints and thereby leave the altitude band, which the cost model checks only at waypoints; with the band enforced along the path, tuned DPF-PSO was significantly better for both numbers of waypoints.",
 "disc_band": "The altitude band of [5] applies at the waypoints only, and encodings that can merge waypoints exploit this: the advantage of tuned SPSO for $n=10$ went with long segments outside the band and turned into a significant disadvantage when the band was enforced along the path.",
 "conc_band": "The advantage of tuned SPSO for 10 waypoints relied on leaving the altitude band between waypoints and was reversed when the band was enforced along the path.",
 "hbd_zh": "SPSO（n = 10：Δ̃ = +6.0%，DPF-PSO 显著更好；n = 20：Δ̃ = +8.2%，DPF-PSO 显著更好）；DE（n = 10：Δ̃ = −0.3%，无显著差异；n = 20：Δ̃ = +6.9%，DPF-PSO 显著更好）；IDP（n = 10：Δ̃ = +0.5%，DPF-PSO 显著更好；n = 20：Δ̃ = −0.2%，无显著差异）",
 "hbt_zh": "tuned SPSO（n = 10：Δ̃ = +2.8%，DPF-PSO 显著更好；n = 20：Δ̃ = +4.6%，DPF-PSO 显著更好）",
 "band_feas_zh": "除 DE（n = 20）400 次运行中的 1 次 外，所有运行都得到可行航迹"
